<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Rai Singh of Bikaner</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1541">1541</a>–<a href="/years/1612">1612</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Rai Singh was raja of Bikaner from 1571 to 1612 and one of the leading <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rajputs">Rajput</a> generals of the Mughal emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/akbar">Akbar</a>, serving in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gujarat">Gujarat</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/deccan">Deccan</a>. He built the Junagarh fort at Bikaner between 1589 and 1594, and his alliance with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mughal-empire">Mughals</a> brought the desert kingdom wealth and high rank.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/rai-singh-of-bikaner.jpg" alt="Rai Singh of Bikaner" width="320" height="428" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: anonymous · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Unknown_artist_-_Portrait_of_Maharaja_Rai_Singh_of_Bikaner_(reigned_1574%E2%80%931612)_-_2021.11_-_Cleveland_Museum_of_Art.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
